              `<strong>Government of India Act 1935 &amp; Independence Act 1947:</strong> The 1935 Act was the blueprint for the Indian Constitution with an All-India Federation, provincial autonomy, three legislative lists, and a Federal Court; the 1947 Act ended British sovereignty, declared India independent from 15 August 1947, and empowered the Constituent Assembly to frame any constitution.`
