            story: `To build a republic from scratch without descending into endless chaos, the Assembly divided its 300+ members into 8 major and 13 minor committees, dividing labor like a giant architectural firm. Nehru steered the Union Powers and Constitution committees, Sardar Patel welded together the Provincial Constitution and Fundamental Rights committees, while Dr. Rajendra Prasad managed the Assembly's rules and steering machinery. Behind the scenes, Constitutional Advisor Sir B.N. Rau traveled the globe, distilling constitutional wisdom from the US, UK, Ireland, and Canada into an initial master draft.`,
