            articles: `1949–1950`,
            summary: `The Constitution was adopted on 26 November 1949 and came into force on 26 January 1950, the date chosen to honour Purna Swaraj.`,
            story: `On 26 November 1949, 284 members signed the completed Constitution, adopting it as the supreme law of the land, while calligraphy artist Prem Behari Narain Raizada beautifully hand-inked the text in flowing italic style. A few urgent articles on citizenship and elections took effect immediately, but the framers deliberately paused full enactment until 26 January 1950. Why? To forever immortalize 26 January 1930, the historic day when the Lahore Congress first raised the Tricolor and declared Purna Swaraj.`,
            storyLink: `With the Constitution enacted, India emerged as the world's most populous constitutional republic, defined by a breathtaking architecture of structural features and schedules.`,
