              `<strong>Adoption &amp; Enforcement:</strong> Adopted on 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day/Samvidhan Divas) and enforced on 26 January 1950 (Republic Day), chosen to commemorate Purna Swaraj Day (26 January 1930, Lahore Session 1929).`,
              `<strong>Immediate Provisions &amp; Original Structure:</strong> Citizenship (Art. 5–9), elections (Art. 324–329), the Provisional Parliament, and temporary/transitional provisions came into force on 26 November 1949; the original Constitution had a Preamble, 395 Articles, 8 Schedules, and 22 Parts; Article 394 governed these immediate provisions, while Article 395 repealed the Indian Independence Act 1947 and the Government of India Act 1935.`,
              `<strong>Signatures:</strong> 284 members signed on 24 January 1950, including 15 women members.`,
