            articles: `10+ Global Sources`,
            summary: `The framers borrowed deliberately: Britain for parliament, the USA for rights and judicial review, Ireland for DPSPs, and Canada for a strong Centre.`,
            story: `Rather than reinventing the wheel in a post-war crisis, Ambedkar and Rau acted as visionary constitutional curators. They borrowed the parliamentary cabinet and rule of law from Britain, the sacred Fundamental Rights and judicial independence from the USA, the compassionate Directive Principles from Ireland, and a robust federal Centre from Canada. From the 1935 Act came two-thirds of the administrative engine, while the Weimar Republic and South Africa contributed emergency suspensions and amendment mechanisms.`,
            storyLink: `To prevent this colossal master document from becoming an unwieldy mess of daily administration, the framers separated operational lists and tables into dedicated Schedules.`,
            points: [
              `<strong>United Kingdom:</strong> Parliamentary government, Rule of Law, legislative procedure, single citizenship, cabinet system, prerogative writs, and bicameralism.`,
              `<strong>United States:</strong> Fundamental Rights, independence of judiciary, judicial review, impeachment of the President, removal of Supreme Court/High Court judges, and Vice-President post.`,
              `<strong>Ireland &amp; Canada:</strong> Ireland gave Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP), nomination of members to the Council of States, and Presidential election method; Canada gave federation with a strong Centre, residuary powers at the Centre, and Governor appointment.`,
              `<strong>Australia, Germany, USSR, France, South Africa &amp; Japan:</strong> Australia (Concurrent List, Joint Sitting); Weimar Germany (suspension of Fundamental Rights during Emergency); USSR (Fundamental Duties &amp; Justice ideals); France (Republic, Liberty-Equality-Fraternity); South Africa (Amendment procedure &amp; Upper House elections); Japan (Procedure established by law).`
            ],
            landmark: `Dr. B.R. Ambedkar emphasized that the Constitution was framed after "ransacking all the known Constitutions of the world" while adapting them to Indian conditions.`,
            takeaway: `Distinguish carefully: Emergency provisions (administrative framework) come from GOI Act 1935, while suspension of Fundamental Rights during Emergency comes from Weimar Germany.`
