            summary: `Schedules 1 to 6 cover states and territories, salaries, oaths, Rajya Sabha seats, Scheduled Areas, and tribal administration.`,
            story: `Imagine needing to update the names of new states, salaries of constitutional dignitaries, or official oaths—putting all that in the main articles would bloat the Constitution. The first six Schedules handle these vital operational foundations: Schedule 1 lists every State and UT; Schedule 2 and 3 fix dignitary salaries and solemn oaths; Schedule 4 allocates Rajya Sabha seats by population to prevent state imbalance. Schedules 5 and 6 provide special administrative autonomy and tribal district councils for Northeast and Scheduled Areas, ensuring tribal customs are shielded from majoritarian bulldozing.`,
            storyLink: `While the first half organizes territorial and institutional basics, the second half of the Schedules tackles high-stakes political battlegrounds: power-sharing lists, languages, and defections.`,
