              `<strong>Classical Languages:</strong> Eleven languages are recognized — Tamil (2004), Sanskrit (2005), Telugu and Kannada (2008), Malayalam (2013), and Odia (2014), plus Marathi, Pali, Prakrit, Assamese, and Bengali added in October 2024.`,
              `<strong>Ninth &amp; Tenth Schedules:</strong> Ninth Schedule added by 1st Amendment (1951) to protect land reform laws (subject to Basic Structure review post-24 April 1973 per I.R. Coelho 2007); Tenth Schedule added by 52nd Amendment (1985) for Anti-Defection.`,
