            articles: `Objectives Resolution`,
            summary: `The Preamble grew out of Nehru's Objectives Resolution and states the source, nature, and aims of the Constitution in one breath.`,
            story: `When a nation of 350 million broke free from 200 years of colonial subjugation, it needed a clear philosophical compass to declare why it existed. On 13 December 1946, Jawaharlal Nehru presented the Objective Resolution, which was later adopted, polished by the Drafting Committee, and placed at the very front as the Preamble. Though debated and finalized at the very end of the Assembly's work to ensure perfect harmony with all articles, it acts as the majestic gateway through which the Indian people declare themselves the ultimate sovereign masters of their own destiny.`,
            storyLink: `This poetic opening declaration fascinated legal scholars and jurists, sparking profound debates over its true constitutional weight and philosophical significance.`,
