              `<strong>Decoration:</strong> The original Preamble was illuminated and decorated by Beohar Rammanohar Sinha and Nandalal Bose of Santiniketan.`,
              `<strong>Four Core Components:</strong> Source of authority ("We, the people of India"); nature of the Indian State (Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic); objectives (Justice, Liberty, Equality, Fraternity); and the date of adoption (26 November 1949).`,
              `<strong>2024 Challenge:</strong> In Ashwini Kumar Upadhyay v. Union of India (November 2024), the Supreme Court rejected a plea challenging the insertion of the words Socialist and Secular by the 42nd Amendment.`
