              `<strong>Pandit Thakur Das Bhargava:</strong> Called it the "Jewel set in the Constitution", the "Soul of the Constitution", the "Most precious part", and the "Yardstick" of the Constitution.`,
              `<strong>Sir Ernest Barker:</strong> Called it the "Keynote of the Constitution" in his book Principles of Social and Political Theory.`,
              `<strong>Justice M. Hidayatullah:</strong> Observed that the Preamble resembles the American Declaration of Independence but is "more than a Declaration".`
            ],
            landmark: `These descriptions are judicial and scholarly characterisations, not separate constitutional provisions.`,
            takeaway: `Remember the four most examined labels: Identity Card (Palkhivala), Political Horoscope (Munshi), Soul/Jewel (Bhargava), and Keynote (Barker).`
