              `<strong>Article 2 vs. Article 3:</strong> Article 2 empowers Parliament to admit or establish new states that were not part of the Union (e.g., Sikkim via 35th &amp; 36th Amendments); Article 3 governs internal readjustment (forming new states, altering area, boundaries, or names of existing states).`,
              `<strong>Article 3 Procedure:</strong> Requires prior President recommendation; the President refers the bill to the concerned State Legislature for views within a specified period (views are non-binding); passed in Parliament by a simple majority.`,
              `<strong>Article 4:</strong> Clarifies that laws enacted under Articles 2 and 3 are NOT deemed constitutional amendments under Article 368.`
