              `<strong>1971–1987:</strong> Himachal Pradesh (1971); Manipur, Tripura, and Meghalaya (21 January 1972); Sikkim became an Associate State by the 35th CAA 1974 and a full State by the 36th CAA 1975; Goa became the 25th State on 30 May 1987 (56th CAA); Arunachal Pradesh (55th CAA) and Mizoram (53rd CAA) became States on 20 February 1987.`,
              `<strong>2000–2019:</strong> Chhattisgarh, Uttarakhand, and Jharkhand were created in November 2000 from Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh, and Bihar; Telangana became the 29th State on 2 June 2014; the Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act 2019 bifurcated J&amp;K into the Union Territories of Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh, abolished the J&amp;K Legislative Council, and left 24 Assembly seats vacant for Pakistan-occupied Kashmir.`
