              `<strong>Article 371A (Nagaland):</strong> Inserted by the 13th CAA 1962; protects Naga customary law, land, and resources and restricts parliamentary laws on religious or social practices, customary law, administration of civil and criminal justice, and ownership of land and resources.`,
              `<strong>Articles 371B–371C:</strong> Article 371B provides for an autonomous State within Assam for certain tribal areas; Article 371C creates a Hill Areas Committee for Manipur.`,
              `<strong>Articles 371D–371F:</strong> Article 371D provides regional reservations and administrative tribunals for Andhra Pradesh and Telangana; Article 371E provides a Central University in Andhra Pradesh; Article 371F contains special safeguards for Sikkim after its accession.`,
              `<strong>Articles 371G–371J:</strong> Article 371G protects Mizo customary law and land; Article 371H gives the Arunachal Pradesh Governor special responsibility for law and order; Article 371-I applies to Goa; Article 371J (98th CAA 2012) provides special development provisions for the Hyderabad-Karnataka region.`
