              `<strong>Doctrine of Waiver:</strong> Citizens cannot voluntarily waive their Fundamental Rights.`,
              `<strong>Article 12 (Definition of State):</strong> Includes the Union and State Governments and Legislatures, local authorities, and statutory or non-statutory authorities under government control; the BCCI and NCERT do not ordinarily fall within Article 12.`,
              `<strong>Article 13 (Judicial Review):</strong> Pre-constitutional laws inconsistent with Fundamental Rights become void under the Doctrine of Eclipse; post-constitutional laws are void ab initio under the Doctrine of Severability; Article 13(4) excludes constitutional amendments from the definition of law (24th CAA 1971).`,
              `<strong>Citizens-Only Rights:</strong> Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, and 30 apply only to citizens; Articles 14, 20, 21, 21A, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, and 28 apply to all persons.`
